\fromosc makes the current pane receive its typing via
OSC, from another LiveLily that uses \sendkeys or
\sendlines. Messages are received at port 9050.
It takes up to one argument, the OSC address to listen to:

\fromosc

Without an argument, the address is /livelily followed by
the number of the pane (counting from 1), for example
/livelily1. An address given as an argument must start
with a /:

\fromosc /mykeys

Messages to the address followed by /press type keys in
the pane, and messages followed by /release release them.
A message can carry integer key codes, or a string whose
characters are typed one by one.
